{"conversation_id":"b7727f50-cada-4c38-8df3-a364422e79f5","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have launched a git history lookup for the `uclass-probe` test row and am waiting for it to finish.\nI have launched the minimal reproduction test and am waiting for its output.\nI have started the two-expression probe in `/tmp/jolt-probe-row.scm` and am waiting for the 5-second watchdog result.\nI have updated `sorted?` in [25-sorted.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/jolt-core/clojure/core/25-sorted.clj#L219-L228) to guard `(instance-check clojure.lang.Sorted x)` with `(jolt.host/jrec-method? x \"seqFrom\")` and launched `sh host/chez/remint.sh` to re-mint the Chez and Gambit seeds. I am waiting for the re-mint to complete before running the verification gates.\nThe seed re-mint completed cleanly. I am now running the minimal reproduction check, `test/chez/sorted-test.ss`, and the four freshness and structural gates (`gambitseedcheck`, `gambitgencheck`, `emittedheads`, `deadhost`).\nThe minimal reproduction check, `sorted-test.ss` (156/156), and all four freshness and structural gates (`gambitseedcheck`, `gambitgencheck`, `emittedheads`, `deadhost`) passed. I have now launched `make CHEZ=\"$JOLT_CHEZ\" unit` and am waiting for the full unit gate to complete.\nThe sandboxed `make unit` run completed without hanging (19/19 `dispatch-caches` passed; 2827/2828 total, with only `winsock`'s `loopback-pair` socket `connect` blocked by the sandbox). I have re-launched `make unit` outside the sandbox to verify 2828/2828 passing and am waiting for it to finish.\nI have completed the root-cause analysis, applied and re-minted the fix in `/Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix`, verified all required gates, and written the full findings report to [1795763090696-engineer-fork-main-unit-hang.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1795763090696-engineer-fork-main-unit-hang.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md).\n\n### 1. Root Cause (**H3 Confirmed**)\n\nThe hang is an unbounded mutual recursion between the fork's `clojure.core/sorted?` ([25-sorted.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/jolt-core/clojure/core/25-sorted.clj#L222)) and upstream's `value-host-tags` class-registration dispatch path ([host-static-classes.ss](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/host/chez/java/host-static-classes.ss#L3547-L3590)), closed after **row 2440** ([unit.edn](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/test/chez/unit.edn#L4255)) installs a `__register-class!` predicate that calls `(not (sorted? x))`:\n\n- **Upstream commit `2573c1807c`** (between `a6852ef8` and `17265497`) changed row 2440 ([unit.edn](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/test/chez/unit.edn#L4255)) from `(fn [x] (and (map? x) (= :uclass-probe (:uclass-kind x)) false))` to `(fn [x] (and (map? x) (not (sorted? x)) (= :uclass-probe (:uclass-kind x)) false))` so later `print-method` rows printing `(sorted-map 1 2)` would not invoke the sorted map's comparator on `:uclass-kind`.\n- When row 2440 runs `(__register-class! pred ...)`, `register-class-arm-checked!` ([host-class.ss](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/host/chez/java/host-class.ss#L34-L37)) probes `pred` on `(class-fast-probes)` **before** `pred` is appended to `jt-user-value-tags-arms` ([host-static-classes.ss](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/host/chez/java/host-static-classes.ss#L3559-L3562)), and `register-class-arm!` bumps `instance-arms-epoch` (invalidating the memo entry computed during the probe). `jt-user-value-tags-arms` is process-wide and is not rolled back by `zj-reset!` ([run-case-isolation.ss](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/host/chez/run-case-isolation.ss#L31-L69)).\n- **Row 2446** ([unit.edn](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/test/chez/unit.edn#L4261)) is the first subsequent row to evaluate `instance?` on a map (`{}`):\n  1. `(instance? clojure.lang.IPersistentMap {})` misses the site and kind caches (because `instance-arms-epoch` was bumped in rows 2440 and 2444) and calls `instance-kind-verdict` ([records-interop.ss](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/host/chez/java/records-interop.ss#L239-L254)) **before** writing to `instance-kind-memo`.\n  2. `instance-kind-verdict` walks the builtin `instance-check-registry` arms ahead of `instance-check-user-arm`, hitting the interface arm at [host-static-classes.ss](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/host/chez/java/host-static-classes.ss#L3583-L3590), which calls `(value-host-tags {})`.\n  3. `value-host-tags` ([host-static-classes.ss](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/host/chez/java/host-static-classes.ss#L3547-L3552)) walks `jt-user-value-tags-arms` first, invoking row 2440's predicate `p` on `{}`.\n  4. Since `(map? {})` is `true`, `p` calls `(sorted? {})`.\n  5. In the fork, `(sorted? {})` evaluates `(or (tree-sorted? {}) (instance-check clojure.lang.Sorted {}))`. Because `instance-arms-epoch` moved after row 2440's probe, `sorted?`'s inline site cache and the `(\"clojure.lang.PersistentArrayMap\", \"clojure.lang.Sorted\")` memo entry are stale, so `instance-kind-entry` calls `(instance-kind-verdict 'clojure.lang.Sorted {})` -\u003e `(value-host-tags {})` -\u003e `p` -\u003e `(sorted? {})` -\u003e `(instance-check clojure.lang.Sorted {})` in an infinite recursion.\n\n### 2. Minimal Reproduction\n\nRunning row 2440's `__register-class!` followed by `(instance? clojure.lang.IPersistentMap {})` via `/tmp/jolt-probe-row.scm` (with a 5s watchdog):\n\n```sh\n\"$JOLT_CHEZ\" --script /tmp/jolt-probe-row.scm '(clojure.core/__register-class! (fn [x] (and (map? x) (not (sorted? x)) (= :uclass-probe (:uclass-kind x)) false)) (fn [_] \"my.Map\") (fn [_] [\"my.Map\"])) (instance? clojure.lang.IPersistentMap {})'\n```\n\n- **Before fix** (exit code 3):\n  ```text\n  HANG (\u003e5s): (clojure.core/__register-class! (fn [x] (and (map? x) (not (sorted? x)) (= :uclass-probe (:uclass-kind x)) false)) (fn [_] \"my.Map\") (fn [_] [\"my.Map\"])) (instance? clojure.lang.IPersistentMap {})\n  ```\n- **After fix** (exit code 0):\n  ```text\n  OK: (clojure.core/__register-class! (fn [x] (and (map? x) (not (sorted? x)) (= :uclass-probe (:uclass-kind x)) false)) (fn [_] \"my.Map\") (fn [_] [\"my.Map\"])) (instance? clojure.lang.IPersistentMap {}) =\u003e true\n  ```\n\n### 3. Fix and Rejected Alternatives\n\n- **Change**: In [25-sorted.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/jolt-core/clojure/core/25-sorted.clj#L219-L228), guarded `(instance-check clojure.lang.Sorted x)` with `(jolt.host/jrec-method? x \"seqFrom\")`:\n  ```clojure\n  (defn sorted? [x]\n    (or (tree-sorted? x)\n        (and (jolt.host/jrec-method? x \"seqFrom\")\n             (instance-check clojure.lang.Sorted x))))\n  ```\n  and re-minted the Chez and Gambit seeds (`sh host/chez/remint.sh`).\n- **Why this is the right place**: It keeps all upstream files untouched and follows the exact pattern of `empty` ([22-coll.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/jolt-core/clojure/core/22-coll.clj#L185)) and `ifn?` ([22-coll.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/jolt-core/clojure/core/22-coll.clj#L245)) using `jolt.host/jrec-method?` ([protocols.ss](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/host/chez/protocols.ss#L409-L413), [records-gambit.ss](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/host/gambit/records-gambit.ss#L2073-L2081)).\n- **Why a naive `(or (jrec? x) (jreify? x))` guard (H1) was rejected**: Every `defrecord` satisfies both `(jrec? r) =\u003e #t` and `(map? r) =\u003e true`. Any later row calling `instance?` or `satisfies?` on a `defrecord` that misses `own-type-declares?` (such as `rdp1.ns` and `rdp5.ns` in [unit.edn](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/test/chez/unit.edn#L4638-L4641)) walks `(value-host-tags r)` -\u003e row 2440's predicate `p` -\u003e `(sorted? r)`. Under a `jrec?`-only guard, `(sorted? r)` would still call `(instance-check clojure.lang.Sorted r)`, miss `own-type-declares?`, and re-enter `(value-host-tags r)` in the exact same infinite recursion. Checking `(jolt.host/jrec-method? x \"seqFrom\")` queries the type's protocol method table directly without `instance-check`.\n\n### 4. Verification Summary\n\nAll required verification gates were run and passed:\n- `sh host/chez/remint.sh`: converged in 2 passes; Chez and Gambit seeds updated.\n- `\"$JOLT_CHEZ\" --script test/chez/sorted-test.ss`: `156/156 passed`.\n- `make CHEZ=\"$JOLT_CHEZ\" GAMBIT_PREFIX=/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/gambit/4.9.8 gambitseedcheck gambitgencheck emittedheads deadhost`: all 4 passed (`gambitseedcheck`, `gambitgencheck`, `emittedheads`, `deadhost`).\n- `make CHEZ=\"$JOLT_CHEZ\" unit`: `unit gate: 2828/2828 passed` (`19/19 dispatch-caches`, `120/120 jvm-misc`, `3/3 r7-rsubseq`, `4/4 r7-sorted-throw`, `2/2 sorted / tree`, `1/1 sorted / subseq laziness`, `2/2 sorted / assoc identity`).\n\n### 5. Residual Risks, Gambit Impact, and Restored `22-coll.clj` Lines\n\n- **Gambit host**: `jolt.host/jrec-method?` is present in [records-gambit.ss](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/host/gambit/records-gambit.ss#L2073-L2081), the Gambit seed was re-minted cleanly, and `gambitseedcheck` / `gambitgencheck` are green.\n- **Residual risk**: Only a vacuous `deftype`/`reify` declaring `clojure.lang.Sorted` without implementing `seqFrom` would return `false` from `sorted?` (the same tradeoff `ifn?` makes with `\"invoke\"`).\n- **Restored `tree-sorted?` lines in [22-coll.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/jolt-syncfix/jolt-core/clojure/core/22-coll.clj#L31) (lines 31 and 189)**: **Must stay.** Both branches immediately dereference `(jolt.host/ref-get m :ops)`, which only exists on Jolt's native B+tree sorted collections (`tree-sorted?`), not on user `deftype`/`reify` implementations of `clojure.lang.Sorted`.\n\nROOT-CAUSE-CONFIRMED\nFIX-VERIFIED\n","duration_seconds":1516.403362,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":412994,"output_tokens":57113,"thinking_tokens":39703,"cache_read_tokens":15201515,"total_tokens"